{
  "_comment": [
    "CANONICAL cross-repo parity fixtures for ReviewSeed's Search Protocol object.",
    "",
    "buildSearchProtocol() folds pool + selections + kwFields + framework + filters +",
    "term provenance + search log into one normalized, serializable record. It is the",
    "seam every report and exporter reads, so both repos must produce byte-equal output:",
    "  - MCP app: server/protocol.ts, imported directly (tests/unit/protocol.test.ts)",
    "  - Website: index.html's page-global buildSearchProtocol, called via Playwright",
    "    page.evaluate (~/code/pubmedseed/tests/verify-parity.mjs)",
    "",
    "BEHAVIOR fixture, hand-written on purpose: these cases encode decisions that a",
    "generated snapshot would silently ratify instead of pinning. The load-bearing ones:",
    "  - an ABSENT `selected` map means 'everything in the pool is selected' (headless",
    "    callers have no selection UI); an EMPTY array means genuinely none selected",
    "  - keywords report their field tag, defaulting to tiab; other kinds report null",
    "  - `latestTotal` is the most recent log entry FOR THIS SOURCE, not the last entry",
    "  - `seedRecords` is deduped in first-seen order walking pools in emission order",
    "  - vocabularies are listed only when that vocabulary's pool is non-empty; ERIC",
    "    carries its pinned snapshot edition, MeSH has none to cite (fetched live)",
    "",
    "The clock is an INPUT (`generatedAt`), never read inside the function — a builder",
    "that reads the wall clock can't be compared across two repos at all.",
    "",
    "Comparison is on canonically-serialized JSON (keys sorted recursively), so key",
    "ORDER may differ between the two implementations but array order may not.",
    "",
    "This file is the single source of truth; the website reads it from this repo",
    "(path via REVIEWSEED_MCP_APP) and is deliberately NOT given a copy. Change shared",
    "protocol behavior here FIRST, then make both repos pass."
  ],
  "version": 1,
